.TH LINUX-THERMAL-CONTROL 1 "2026-08-19" "linux-thermal-control 0.5.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux-thermal-control \- capability-aware Linux thermal controller
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-thermal-control
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the unprivileged Qt Quick client. Hardware discovery, telemetry and fan
writes are performed by a privileged daemon through system D-Bus. Control
requests require Polkit authorization.
.PP
Closing the main window hides it to the Linux system tray and keeps the client
running. Use the tray menu's Exit action to terminate the client. If the desktop
does not provide a system tray, normal close behavior is retained so the window
cannot become inaccessible.
.SH TRAY MENU
.TP
.B Show Main Window
Show, raise and activate the main window.
.TP
.B Hide Main Window
Hide the main window while keeping the client running.
.TP
.B Exit
Hide the tray icon and terminate the graphical client.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B automatic
Return each supported fan zone to its kernel-driver, firmware or controller
automatic mode.
.TP
.B full-speed
Set every controllable fan zone to its supported maximum. Read-only fans are
not written.
.TP
.B custom-curve
Apply saved per-zone temperature curves with sensor-failure and safety endpoint
protection.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/linux-thermal-control/curves.json
Persisted per-zone curve profiles.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/linux-thermal-daemon.service
Privileged hardware-control daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR sensors (1),
.BR pkcheck (1)
